================================================================================
1. SQLite -- upstream amalgamation, compiled and shipped
================================================================================

  Component:  SQLite 3.53.4 amalgamation (sqlite3.c, sqlite3.h)
  Origin:     https://sqlite.org/2026/sqlite-amalgamation-3530400.zip
  Pinned in:  sqlite-version.lock (SHA256 and upstream's published SHA3-256)
  License:    Public domain
  Modified:   No. Compiled unmodified; configuration is by -D flags only
              (build/flags.sh), which is what SQLite's own build system does.
  Shipped in: lib/darwin_arm64/libsqlite3.dylib
              lib/linux_amd64/libsqlite3.so

SQLite's authors place it in the public domain. Every source file in the
amalgamation carries this dedication in place of a legal notice:

     The author disclaims copyright to this source code.  In place of
     a legal notice, here is a blessing:

        May you do good and not evil.
        May you find forgiveness for yourself and forgive others.
        May you share freely, never taking more than you give.

The amalgamation source is not committed to this repository. build/fetch.sh
downloads it from sqlite.org and verifies both hashes before unpacking; the
unpacked tree lives in build/upstream/, which is gitignored. What this
repository commits is the compiled result.


================================================================================
2. sqlite-vec -- optional extension, compiled into the shipped libraries
================================================================================

  Component:  sqlite-vec 0.1.9 (sqlite-vec.c, sqlite-vec.h)
  Author:     Alex Garcia (asg017)
  Origin:     https://github.com/asg017/sqlite-vec
  Pinned in:  build/extensions.lock (SHA256)
  License:    Dual-licensed Apache-2.0 OR MIT, at the recipient's option.
              This distribution elects MIT.
  Modified:   No. Compiled unmodified with -DSQLITE_VEC_STATIC -DSQLITE_CORE.
  Shipped in: lib/darwin_arm64/libsqlite3.dylib
              lib/linux_amd64/libsqlite3.so

License texts: third_party/sqlite-vec/LICENSE-MIT (the one elected here)
               third_party/sqlite-vec/LICENSE-APACHE (the alternative, for
               recipients who prefer to take it under Apache-2.0)

  MIT License
  Copyright (c) 2024 Alex Garcia

Read this carefully, because the default in the build scripts and the content
of the committed libraries are not the same thing:

  - `make build` builds WITHOUT sqlite-vec. That is the source-build default.
  - The libraries COMMITTED under lib/ were built WITH it, by
    `WITH_SQLITE_VEC=1 make build` (equivalently `make ship-lib`).

So a consumer who takes the prebuilt library -- which is the normal path, and
the one `go get` gives you -- receives sqlite-vec's compiled code, and the MIT
notice above travels with it. `sqlite3.CompiledExtensions()` reports at runtime
what the loaded library actually carries.


